+## 18. Colour roles for code, links and quotes (2026-11-18)
+
+Local patch, not upstream. Inline code, code blocks, links and block quotes had fixed ANSI
+colours in `layout.rs`, so a `[colors]` theme could not reach them. They are now palette
+roles, `code`, `code-block`, `link` and `quote`, with the old colours as the default in both
+palettes; links stay underlined and quotes italic whatever colour is set.
+
+`tui-markdown` 0.3.9 has one `StyleSheet::code()` for both kinds of code. It puts it on the
+span for inline code and on the line for a block, and on no line at all once syntax
+highlighting is compiled in. So which lines belong to a code block is decided
+from the parse, not from the renderer's styling: every line of a top-level code block, and,
+in a list or quote, every line whose text maps into a code block the container parse
+(`decorate::Syntax`) already walks. Such a line's style becomes the `code-block` colour;
+inline code keeps `code` on its own span. Highlighted code keeps its theme's colours,
+which sit on the spans and win over the line's.
